##  Sections of the QNX Photon shelf, top to bottom.
##
##  Read by bin/shelf-panel, which draws the whole sidebar in one window.
##  There is no generator any more: the panel lays itself out at runtime, so
##  a section's height is whatever its contents come to rather than a number
##  someone has to solve in advance.  Adding a row means adding a line.
##
##  Format, one directive per line:
##
##    group <Label>        starts a collapsible group.  The label is also the
##                         handle used in the state file, so keep it stable.
##    item <Label> | <icon> | <command>
##                         a launcher row.  <icon> is a file in icons/, or a
##                         themed name looked up in the Haiku set.  <command>
##                         is run through the shell.
##    widget <name>        a drawn widget: worldview, meters, media, tasks,
##                         tray or clock.
##    bare <name>          a widget section with no group header at all, so
##                         it cannot be collapsed and costs no HEADER_H --
##                         for a section that should read as part of the
##                         frame rather than a titled group, like the clock.
##    flex                 marks the group *above* as the one that absorbs
##                         the panel's leftover height.  Sections above it
##                         stack from the top as usual; sections below it
##                         are pinned to the bottom of the panel instead;
##                         the flex group is given whatever vertical space
##                         is left between the two, never less than its own
##                         natural height.  At most one group should carry
##                         this -- a spec with none falls back to the old
##                         top-down stack with a sunken filler at the bottom.
##
##  $VARS in a command are expanded by the shell that runs it, so the
##  terminal and friends come from the environment rather than from fvwm's
##  InfoStore -- bin/shelf-panel is not an fvwm module and cannot read it.

##  The launchers are parked, not gone.  LauncherBody and the `item`
##  directive both still work; uncommenting a group below is all it takes to
##  bring the rows back.
#
#group Applications
#item Terminal     | 16x16-xterm-color.png                    | ${TERMINAL:-kitty}
#item Browser      | 16x16-firefox.png                        | firefox
#item File Manager | 16x16-Explorer++.png                     | ${FILEMANAGER:-dolphin}
#item Calculator   | 16x16-org.speedcrunch.SpeedCrunch.png    | ${CALCULATOR:-speedcrunch}
#item Editor       | 16x16-emacs.png                          | emacs
#
#group Utilities
#item Process Monitor | 16x16-qps.png                         | ${TERMINAL:-kitty} -e btop
#item Screenshot      | 16x16-org.flameshot.Flameshot.png     | flameshot gui
#item Clipboard       | 16x16-qlipper.png                     | qlipper
#
#group Configure
#item Graphics     | 16x16-nvidia-settings.png                | arandr
#item Screen Saver | 16x16-xscreensaver.png                   | xscreensaver-demo
#item Appearance   | 16x16-menulibre.png                      | ${TERMINAL:-kitty} -e ${EDITOR:-vi} $FVWM_USERDIR/config

##  Windows absorbs whatever the rest of the stack does not need -- the same
##  job FvwmTaskBar's window-list cell did, now with a whole sidebar's worth
##  of height to grow into instead of one fixed row.
group Windows
widget tasks
flex

group System Tray
widget tray

group World View
widget worldview

group System Monitor
widget meters

group Media
widget media

##  No header: flush against the bottom of the panel, the last thing in the
##  stack.  Format and position both carried over from TaskbarClockTick.
bare clock
